    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d878">

                <pb facs="0753" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/8641</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2715</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-15">January 15, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received January
                        16.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the Department’s telegram No. 3, of January 13, 1940, and to report that I
                    shall take the first opportunity to inform the Cuban Ambassador to Washington in
                    the sense indicated.</p>
                <p>I am sure the Department understands that the Embassy has made every effort to
                    refrain from becoming involved in the present unsatisfactory electoral
                    situation. In accordance with this policy, it has occurred to me—bearing in mind
                    that the Cuban Ambassador to Washington, while personally friendly to General
                    Menocal, is considered by the latter, and particularly by his followers, as a
                    member of the government coalition—that it might become desirable, in the <pb
                        facs="0754" n="742" xml:id="pg742"/> interest of keeping our Government from
                    becoming involved in this domestic situation, for me to transmit directly to
                    General Menocal, or to Dr. Cuervo Rubio,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d878-f1"/> the
                    information contained in the Department’s telegram referred to.</p>
                <p>If the Department agrees, I shall be glad to receive instructions to transmit
                    this information to the persons indicated, should it appear desirable to do
                    so.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard L.
                    Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
